med-device-eu pack: content licence
====================================

This file governs the content of this pack (SKILL.md, chapters/,
glossary.md, cheatsheet.md). The repository's MIT licence covers tooling
and scaffolding only. The pack ships original reconstructed reference
notes with attribution; the guidance documents themselves and the official
PDFs are not redistributed.

1. Attribution statement

The six sources carry two public-sector grants. The five MDCG documents
(S1 to S5) are European Commission material reused under the Commission's
reuse policy, Decision 2011/833/EU, which licenses Commission content
under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
(CC BY 4.0) unless otherwise indicated. The MHRA guidance (S6) is UK
public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence
v3.0.

CC BY 4.0 deed: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
OGL v3 deed: https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/

2. European Commission reuse statement

The MDCG documents are reused under the European Commission's reuse
policy, Decision 2011/833/EU of 12 December 2011 on the reuse of
Commission documents. Reuse of Commission documents is authorised under
that decision, subject to its terms, provided the source is appropriately
credited and changes are indicated. This pack credits each document in
section 5, and the indication of changes required by the decision is
satisfied by the change_indication field of PACK.yaml ("reconstructed as
synthesized reference notes"): the pack is synthesized notes with
attribution and reproduces no guidance text.

Commission-side source links, which serve attribution only. The Open
Government Licence does not cover Commission documents, so these two
links are not OGL condition links:

Endorsed-guidance index: https://health.ec.europa.eu/medical-devices-sector/new-regulations/guidance-mdcg-endorsed-documents-and-other-guidance_en
Commission legal notice: https://commission.europa.eu/legal-notice_en

3. Open Government Licence v3.0 attribution (MHRA)

Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.

Source of the MHRA information, as the OGL acknowledgement condition
requires:

Publication page: https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/medical-devices-software-applications-apps
OGL v3 deed: https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/

4. Non-endorsement and publisher disclaimers

The European Commission does not endorse this pack. The Medicines and
Healthcare products Regulatory Agency (MHRA) does not endorse this pack.
Neither publisher has any official status in relation to it.

MDCG status statement, recorded as the publisher's own disclaimer, stated
in the PDFs (page 1 of each MDCG document, S1 to S5) and copied from the
capture record: "Any views expressed in this document are not legally
binding and only the Court of Justice of the European Union can give
binding interpretations of Union law." That sentence is the publishers'
statement about the guidance's legal status; it is not a licence
restriction.

5. Per-source record

One block per source, S1 to S6, each with the in-source licence statement
from the capture record. "Used in" names this pack's chapters.

